#### B. The File Download API
For the download endpoint, you format it exactly as you drafted. You chain the headers directly onto the ResponseEntity.ok() builder, instructing the browser to download the byte array as an attachment.
```java
    @GetMapping("/download-batch/{batchId}")
    public ResponseEntity<byte[]> downloadBatch(@PathVariable String batchId) {
        try {
            // 1. Get the byte array from your service
            byte[] fileData = voucherRequestService.generateBatchExcel(batchId);
            
            // 2. Return with strict attachment and anti-sniffing headers
            return ResponseEntity.ok()
                    .header(org.springframework.http.HttpHeaders.CONTENT_DISPOSITION, "attachment; filename=\"Batch_" + batchId + ".xlsx\"")
                    .header(org.springframework.http.HttpHeaders.CONTENT_TYPE, "application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet")
                    .header("X-Content-Type-Options", "nosniff")
                    .header(org.springframework.http.HttpHeaders.CACHE_CONTROL, "no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate")
                    .body(fileData);
                    
        } catch (Exception e) {
            // If download fails, return 400 Bad Request
            return ResponseEntity.badRequest().build();
        }
    }

